<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! carriage.fresher.reads ~ working copies over a canon bag that moved past their base

`lares vessel fresher --bag <slug>` reads each working copy over that canon bag that shadows fresher canon, its base hash beside canon's, then each copy with no base that differs from canon. It writes nothing.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ fresher

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`fresher` params=`bag/lares ~ the copies shadowing fresher lares canon`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ bag

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`bag` params=`takes/slug needs/required ~ the canon bag, a slug or lar:///ha.ka.ba/bags/<slug>`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ local

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`local` params=`who/seat-or-hand ~ runs on this host's own vessel root; this handler checks no ocap`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

